&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;## 職務内容&lt;br&gt;PlayStationの製造に関わるミッションクリティカルなシステムの設計・開発・運用保守において、担当領域のエンジニアリングチームをリードするマネジメント業務を担当いただきます。&lt;br&gt;担当システムは、高いセキュリティ・可用性・品質が求められるミッションクリティカルな環境です。 &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;ハードウェア設計・製造・サプライチェーンなど、多様な領域のステークホルダーと連携しながら、グローバル規模でシステムを展開しています。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- &amp;nbsp;ステークホルダー（主にPlayStation製品の設計・製造部門）からの要求事項分析およびシステム要件定義&lt;br&gt;- 要件に基づき、オンプレミス環境を中心としたインフラおよびソフトウェアの設計・開発・実装・テストを、外部パートナーと連携しながら推進&lt;br&gt;- インフラおよびソフトウェア設計・開発の知見を活かし、システム全体の効率化および最適化に貢献&lt;br&gt;- 担当領域（Manufacturing IT）のシステム開発・運用において、技術的な意思決定および課題解決をリード&lt;br&gt;- オンプレミス環境におけるコンテナ基盤を前提としたインフラアーキテクチャ設計および運用戦略の策定・推進&lt;br&gt;- PICSYの拡張・機能改善、および次世代製品対応に向けたシステム改修の推進&lt;br&gt;- セキュリティ要件（InfoSec / ProdSec）に準拠した設計・実装の推進（暗号化・鍵管理・HSM等含む）&lt;br&gt;- ミッションクリティカルなシステムの安定運用・保守管理をリードし、障害対応・原因分析・再発防止・継続的改善を推進&lt;br&gt;- 外部パートナーの管理・調整および品質・納期の担保&lt;br&gt;- 担当チームのマネジメント（タスク管理、育成、パフォーマンス管理）&lt;br&gt;- 自動化・標準化を含む運用プロセス改善の推進&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;---&lt;br&gt;## 組織・職場紹介&lt;br&gt;- PlayStationビジネスにおける各種課題に対して、主にITの側面からソリューション提供を行う組織です。&lt;br&gt;- ITサービスはグローバルで展開しており、各地域の担当者とコミュニケーションを取り、日本・アジア地域に最適なものを提供できるよう尽力しています。&lt;br&gt;- メンバーは多様なスキル・経験を持ち、互いに教えあい・学びあうことで成長し、組織に貢献できるチームワークが醸成されています。また、自主性を重んじたチーム運営がなされており、チャレンジしやすい環境です。&lt;br&gt;- 業務はテレワークと出社のハイブリッドで実施しています。出社は強制ではなく、各人の生活状況に応じて選択可能です。新規メンバーが加わる際には、チームビルディングも兼ねて積極的に出社し、迎え入れる体制があります。&lt;br&gt;- PlayStationビジネスを通じてキャリア開発・スキル向上を図り、組織および会社への貢献を目指す方にとって、成長機会の多い環境です。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;---&lt;br&gt;## 応募資格&lt;br&gt;### **【必須（MUST）】**&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- ITシステムにおける設計/開発/保守運用経験（10年以上）&lt;br&gt;- 事業継続性に影響を与えるミッションクリティカルなシステムにおいて、運用保守（障害対応・原因分析・再発防止を含む）を主体的にリードした経験&lt;br&gt;- エンジニアリングチームのリードまたはマネジメント経験&lt;br&gt;- オンプレミス環境におけるインフラ設計・構築・運用経験（高可用性設計、障害耐性設計を含む）&lt;br&gt;- Linuxベースのサーバー環境における設計・運用経験&lt;br&gt;- コンテナ基盤（Kubernetes等）の設計・構築・運用経験（オンプレ環境）&lt;br&gt;- システムの非機能要件（可用性・性能・セキュリティ）を考慮したアーキテクチャ設計経験&lt;br&gt;- 監視・ログ分析等を活用したシステム運用改善経験&lt;br&gt;- リレーショナルデータベースを利用した開発または運用経験&lt;br&gt;- 外部パートナーと連携した開発・運用経験&lt;br&gt;- 語学&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- 英語：英語での会議、設計レビュー、技術ドキュメント作成が可能なコミュニケーション能力&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- 日本語：ネイティブレベル &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;---&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;### **【歓迎（WANT）】**&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- **DR/BCP設計・運用経験（RTO/RPO設計・テスト含む）**&lt;br&gt;- **セキュリティ領域の経験（IAM / 暗号化 / HSM / ネットワークセキュリティ等）**&lt;br&gt;- **IaC（Terraform / Ansible 等）によるインフラ管理経験**&lt;br&gt;- 製造系ITシステムの設計/開発/保守運用経験&lt;br&gt;- 大規模システムにおけるインシデント管理・運用改善の経験&lt;br&gt;- ハードウェアの設計開発経験&lt;br&gt;- PlayStationやゲームへの興味・関心&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;---&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;## 求める人物像&lt;br&gt;- 技術への探究心が強く、新しいIT技術の習得に積極的に取り組める方&lt;br&gt;- 多様な手段で正確かつ円滑にコミュニケーションできる方 &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;- 常に利用者視点を持ち、ユーザーの立場からシステムや機能を設計できる方 &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;- 状況に応じてリーダーシップを発揮し、周囲を巻き込んで業務を推進できる方 &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;- 新たな価値や仕組みを創出する意欲と志を持って取り組める方&lt;br&gt;- 不確実性の高い状況でも、自ら課題を整理し、主体的に推進できる方&lt;br&gt;- 多様なメンバーと相互に尊重し合い、チームとして協力しながら課題解決に取り組める方&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment is a Fair Chance employer and qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records will be considered for employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Principal Program Manager, Cloud Streaming&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is seeking an experienced Principal Program Manager to lead complex, high-impact programs across the PlayStation ecosystem. This role is central to driving cross-functional execution at scale, bringing together teams across technology, product, business, and operations to deliver meaningful outcomes for players worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As both a strategist and executor, the Principal Program Manager will shape program direction, create clarity in complex and ambiguous environments, and drive programs from strategy through execution, launch, and value realization. This leader will anticipate challenges, bring forward clear recommendations, and influence decisions across diverse global teams and senior leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Program Leadership&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead geographically distributed, cross-functional teams in delivering large-scale programs from strategy and definition through execution, launch, and ongoing value realization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate strategic objectives into clear program outcomes, priorities, milestones, success measures, and execution plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive end-to-end program outcomes, connecting business objectives, product strategy, technology delivery, and operational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create structure and clarity in complex or ambiguous environments, ensuring teams remain aligned on priorities, ownership, and desired outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted program voice to executives and stakeholders, providing clear visibility into program health, priorities, risks, and decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Strategic Program Management&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and influence program delivery strategies that balance speed, quality, scalability, investment, and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish effective program structures, governance, operating rhythms, and decision-making frameworks appropriate to the scale and complexity of the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a broad perspective across the program, anticipating emerging risks, dependencies, opportunities, and decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate ambiguity with sound judgment, clearly communicating trade-offs and recommendations to senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt plans as business, technology, and customer needs evolve while maintaining focus on overall program outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply and evolve program management best practices to improve predictability, execution, and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Collaboration&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong partnerships across Engineering, Product Management, Design, Quality, Operations, Business, and other functions required to deliver program outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence effectively across teams and organizational boundaries, including in situations where priorities, perspectives, or incentives differ.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify risks and opportunities, framing complex issues clearly and bringing forward options and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize complex information into concise, actionable communication for senior leaders and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish transparent, data-driven reporting that provides a reliable source of truth for program health and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster shared ownership and accountability across teams, ensuring actions and decisions are driven through to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Organizational Impact &amp;amp; Innovation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to simplify ways of working, reduce unnecessary overhead, and accelerate cross-functional execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and apply scalable approaches, frameworks, and best practices that strengthen program delivery beyond an individual initiative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data, insights, and measurable outcomes to evaluate program effectiveness and inform decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge existing approaches where appropriate and help teams continuously improve how they plan, collaborate, and deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide leadership, mentorship, and guidance to Program Managers and Technical Program Managers supporting the program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Where applicable, provide strategic oversight of a broader program management team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Culture&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act with ownership, accountability, urgency, and strong judgment in delivering results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create an environment where teams can openly surface risks, challenge assumptions, and work through difficult issues constructively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourage diverse perspectives and inclusive collaboration across global teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance respect for established systems and practices with a forward-looking mindset and a willingness to drive meaningful change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model collaborative leadership and help others operate with greater clarity, confidence, and ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent relevant professional experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience leading large-scale, complex technology or consumer-facing programs across multiple functions and organizational boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading programs across one or more areas such as software, hardware, platforms, services, infrastructure, digital experiences, or business capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to operate effectively in complex and ambiguous environments and translate strategic objectives into executable programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience establishing program structures, governance models, operating rhythms, and decision-making frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to identify and communicate risks, options, trade-offs, and recommendations to senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence senior executives and work effectively across multiple organizational levels without relying on direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to simplify complex information and focus audiences on the decisions and outcomes that matter most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using data, metrics, and measurable outcomes to assess program health, guide decisions, and evaluate impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong critical thinking and judgment, with the ability to connect near-term execution to broader business and organizational objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience providing leadership, mentorship, or guidance to other program management professionals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at working across diverse, geographically distributed teams and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the gaming, digital entertainment, or consumer technology industry preferred, but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At SIE, we consider several factors when setting each role’s base pay range, including the competitive benchmarking data for the market and geographic location.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note that the base pay range may vary in line with our hybrid working policy and individual base pay will be determined based on job-related factors which may include knowledge, skills, experience, and location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition, this role &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;is eligible&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; for SIE’s top-tier benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, matching 401(k), paid time off, wellness program and coveted employee discounts for Sony products. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This role also may be eligible for a bonus package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Click&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.playstation.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; to learn more.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The estimated base pay range for this role is listed below.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$220,900&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$331,300 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment is a Fair Chance employer and qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records will be considered for employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal TPM - GSO Studio Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;United States, Remote&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Vice President of GSO and Studio Enablement, the Principal Technical Program Manager (TPM) will serve as a key driver of strategy, execution, and organizational alignment across one of Sony Interactive Entertainment’s most critical technology domains. This role is an individual contributor with significant influence, operating at the intersection of engineering, product, and business stakeholders.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Principal TPM will shape and advance initiatives across Global Service Operations and Studio IT, ensuring both organizations’ missions. The role requires not only deep technical program management expertise but also organizational design insight, executive-level communication, and the ability to foster alignment across leadership teams, operating companies, and external partners.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is a high-impact role for a seasoned technical program leader who thrives in complexity, navigates ambiguity, and builds trust at all levels of the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strategic Program Leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate GSO and Studio Enablement’s long-term strategy into clear execution roadmaps, working across engineering, product, and operations teams to drive delivery of mission-critical initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate and surface cross-organizational dependencies, risks, and trade-offs, guiding leadership decision-making with data, insight, and scenario planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cross-Organizational Influence &amp;amp; Stakeholder Engagement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with leaders across SIE engineering, product management, design, and operations to align priorities and unlock execution velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent GSO and Studio Enablement in enterprise forums, ensuring that operations and studio IT capabilities are positioned effectively across Sony’s ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with external stakeholders (partners, vendors, strategic alliances) to accelerate adoption of Studio IT capabilities and extend GSO value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Execution Excellence &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive program governance for our highest-priority initiatives, ensuring effective rhythm-of-business, transparent reporting, and predictable execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success metrics and KPIs for our programs, producing data-driven insights that inform leadership decisions and drive accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish operating frameworks that simplify decision-making and improve organizational agility across multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Organizational Design &amp;amp; Enablement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a thought partner to team leadership, helping design and refine organizational structures, roles, and processes that enable sustainable growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curate leadership offsites, reviews, and cross-functional planning forums that sharpen objectives and unify execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion modern engineering and program management practices (Agile, SAFe, Lean Portfolio Management) that enhance collaboration, delivery predictability, and organizational health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Executive Communication &amp;amp; Storytelling&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft clear, compelling communications (strategy narratives, board/executive briefings, external partner messaging) that connect our technical vision to business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Elevate GSO and Studio Enablement’s voice across Sony and the industry by supporting leadership with thought leadership, positioning, and strategic storytelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure visibility and alignment by producing high-quality reports, presentations, and narratives for executives across Sony’s operating companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Expertise&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in technical program management, portfolio management, or related roles in large-scale software environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of leading high-impact programs across global, matrixed organizations and aligning technical execution to business strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with shared IT platforms and services across larger organizations, including modernization and standardization efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of cloud platforms, networking, distributed systems, and infrastructure operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using automation, telemetry, and emerging AI capabilities to reduce manual work and improve support outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CI/CD, engineering tooling, platform services, and improving developer workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience helping teams move from reactive support toward more proactive, repeatable, and automated operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence without direct authority, with a history of driving alignment across senior executives and distributed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written, verbal, and visual communication skills; adept at tailoring messages for executive and technical audiences alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience guiding executive stakeholders through organizational change, re-org planning, and enterprise-scale transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to act as a trusted partner to senior leaders, balancing strategic insight with operational rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting production systems, incident response, reliability, monitoring, and operational improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting studio technology, developer environments, build workflows, source control, and day-to-day production needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or advanced degree preferred, but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certifications in Agile, SAFe, or PMP are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Success Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate as a strategic integrator—connecting vision to execution across multiple organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a catalyst for alignment—building clarity and trust across executive teams and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate chief-of-staff-like influence—shaping organizational design, communication, and leadership effectiveness while remaining grounded in technical program management excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in a global, fast-paced, and ambiguous environment, always bringing a collaborative, outcome-driven mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-KS1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At SIE, we consider several factors when setting each role’s base pay range, including the competitive benchmarking data for the market and geographic location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Please note that the base pay range may vary in line with our hybrid working policy and individual base pay will be determined based on job-related factors which may include knowledge, skills, experience, and location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;In addition, this role is eligible for SIE’s top-tier benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, matching 401(k), paid time off, wellness program and coveted employee discounts for Sony products. This role also may be eligible for a bonus package. Click &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.playstation.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; to learn more.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;This is a flexible role that can be remote, with varying pay ranges based on geographic location. For example, if you are based out of Seattle, the estimated base pay range for this role is listed below.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$236,300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$354,500 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment is a Fair Chance employer and qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records will be considered for employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Wireless Protocol Architect/Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building a small team of versatile and enthusiastic leaders to create new products for the PlayStation community. Our team recently delivered the new PlayStation Link, PULSE Explore and PULSE Elite products, recently announced the FlexStrike and PULSE Elevate products, and are hard at work on what comes next. We need an experienced and innovative firmware engineer to help build and support our new products and features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will be the technical point of accountability for wireless across accessories: hardware, platform software, audio, security, and product all will route protocol questions to you. You will represent the protocol and the implementation to silicon and ODM partners, evaluate combo-SoC roadmaps, drive vendor firmware defects to resolution, and design so that a supplier change is a port, not a rewrite.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will write the technical strategy documents that let a Director and a VP make an informed decision. And, grow the technical depth by being the leader that mentors senior engineers toward staff and principal, and raise the design-review bar for the whole org.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Come and play with us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will lead firmware development for high profile product development efforts. You will be responsible for technical leadership, system architecture, and&amp;nbsp;execution across the firmware domain, working closely with internal teams and external partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own firmware architecture and design for transport, wireless protocol, firmware and software stacks for embedded devices from concept through production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and define communication protocols to enable peripheral functionality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and scale low-latency RF/wireless communication protocols for embedded systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect structured, modular, and reusable firmware frameworks that scale across multiple platforms and product lines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and mentor firmware engineers (internal and external partners)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure firmware designs support cross-platform reuse and long-term scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot complex system-level issues across hardware, firmware, and RF domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong in firmware and software architectural patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong embedded firmware development experience in C/C++&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry authority level experience with RF/wireless systems (e.g., Bluetooth, low-latency audio, or similar technologies)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of low-latency embedded systems and communication protocol design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to design scalable, reusable, and cross-platform firmware architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ARM microcontrollers and low-power system design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with hardware bring-up and debugging (including RF/system-level issues)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing hardware-in-the-loop and automated testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong system-level thinking across hardware and software boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate at both high-level system design and low-level implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead firmware efforts across teams and partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with consumer electronics product development from concept through mass production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and debugging skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in electrical engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or related field (or equivalent experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in embedded firmware development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading firmware development for shipped products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in RF/wireless or low-latency embedded systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for gaming, digital entertainment, and consumer electronics is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with wireless audio or ultra-low latency systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with external development partners or ODMs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with kernel or driver development (Linux, Windows, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling engineering processes and mentoring teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Conditions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Energetic, collaborative and passionate engineers delivering product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel (domestic and international) required. Estimated 15-20%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At SIE, we consider several factors when setting each role’s base pay range, including the competitive benchmarking data for the market and geographic location.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note that the base pay range may vary in line with our hybrid working policy and individual base pay will be determined based on job-related factors which may include knowledge, skills, experience, and location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition, this role &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;is eligible&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; for SIE’s top-tier benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, matching 401(k), paid time off, wellness program and coveted employee discounts for Sony products. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This role also may be eligible for a bonus package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Click&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.playstation.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; to learn more.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The estimated base pay range for this role is listed below.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$209,900&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$314,900 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
