&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment is a Fair Chance employer and qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records will be considered for employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Senior Event Planner, Global Events &amp;amp; Activations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;San Mateo, CA (Hybrid/Collab)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Position Summary&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Event Planner is an experienced event marketer responsible for supporting the Global Events &amp;amp; Activations team in translating marketing objectives into world-class live experiences that support commercial goals, strengthen brand perception and create meaningful engagement with players.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Senior Manager, Global Events &amp;amp; Activations, this role will own the end-to-end development of events &amp;amp; activations for assigned campaigns, from initial briefing and planning through agency management, production, global rollout and post-campaign evaluation. The role will work collaboratively with Global Marketing, Game Studios, PR, Social, Partnership, Influencer and Territory Marketing teams to ensure every activation delivers against a unified global vision while allowing flexibility for local market execution.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is a highly collaborative role requiring equal strengths in marketing judgement, creative development and production leadership. Success will come from the ability to influence stakeholders, simplify complexity and confidently lead programs that inspire audiences across the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event &amp;amp; Production Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead assigned activation initiatives for global marketing campaigns, many with a U.S. focus, from briefing through delivery and evaluation, translating marketing objectives into clear and actionable plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Games Marketing, Brand and Hardware Marketing, Studios, Partnerships, Sponsorships, PR, Social, Influencer and Territory Marketing teams to define the role of events within broader go-to-market plans and identify opportunities for creators, content and earned media.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop events briefs and guide agencies from concept through programming, production and live delivery, balancing creative ambition with budget, timeline and operational feasibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage agencies, suppliers, budgets, statements of work, schedules and technical or onsite operations to deliver high-quality experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Enablement &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present activation frameworks to territory teams, review local proposals and provide guidance that maintains a unified global vision while allowing appropriate market flexibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure programs meet Creative, Legal, Corporate Security and Health &amp;amp; Safety requirements, supported by clear risk assessments, operational plans and delivery schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measurement &amp;amp; Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define KPIs, lead post-event reporting and share insights and recommendations that strengthen future campaigns and the Global Events &amp;amp; Activations Strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approximately 8+ years of relevant experience in experiential marketing, events or production within gaming, entertainment, media or technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading global experiential campaigns from strategy and creative development through production, rollout and evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong integrated marketing, stakeholder and agency management skills, including the ability to influence senior partners and build trusted relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial awareness and production expertise, including budgets, suppliers, governance, risk assessments and Health &amp;amp; Safety requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance strategic thinking and creative ambition with operational feasibility, timelines and business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, confident communicator who is equally comfortable presenting to senior leadership as well as supporting onsite delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At SIE, we consider several factors when setting each role’s base pay range, including the competitive benchmarking data for the market and geographic location.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note that the base pay range may vary in line with our hybrid working policy and individual base pay will be determined based on job-related factors which may include knowledge, skills, experience, and location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition, this role &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;is eligible&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; for SIE’s top-tier benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, matching 401(k), paid time off, wellness program and coveted employee discounts for Sony products. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This role also may be eligible for a bonus package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Click&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.playstation.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; to learn more.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The estimated base pay range for this role is listed below.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$146,400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$219,600 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment is a Fair Chance employer and qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records will be considered for employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #365f91;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Senior Executive Assistant, Legal, Public Policy &amp;amp; ESG&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;San Mateo, CA&amp;nbsp;| &lt;/strong&gt;Hybrid -&lt;strong&gt; 2+ days per week in our San Mateo office&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Role Summary:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Are you ready to step into the heart of PlayStation’s global Legal, Public Policy &amp;amp; ESG team and make a real impact? As the Senior Executive Assistant to the Senior Vice President &amp;amp; General Counsel at Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE), you’ll do far more than manage calendars and schedules, you’ll be a trusted partner, culture-builder, and the glue that keeps a dynamic, global organization moving at full speed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;This role is perfect for someone who thrives on variety and challenge. One day, you may be orchestrating a high-profile global legal summit or a creative offsite retreat; the next, you might be coordinating across time zones to ensure seamless collaboration between teams spanning continents. You’ll flex your project management skills, design memorable experiences that bring people together, and support a leader who is reshaping how Legal, Public Policy &amp;amp; ESG, drives impact at one of the world’s most iconic entertainment brands.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Because our General Counsel’s role is global, you’ll work alongside a passionate, collaborative team that embodies innovation, creativity, and inclusion. If you’re energized by fast paced environments and want to help shape not just the future of PlayStation, but what’s possible at the intersection of law, tech, and entertainment, we’d love to hear from you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Handle swiftly and without error a complex and ever-changing calendar for the General Counsel; prepare for and coordinate meetings, and schedule travel plans and accommodations for the Executive and the department, as assigned.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Ensure a timely flow of information, obtain signatures and authorizations, answer and screen phone calls and manage correspondence and communication flow. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Submit expense reports for the General Counsel and department team, as assigned. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Process outside counsel invoices, sending communications on behalf of the General Counsel. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Professionally represent the Executive through initial contact meetings or telephone conversations. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Act as administrative liaison between the Executive and Sony groups, vendors, and industry contacts. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Provide logistical support for department team meetings, events, and conferences, working in collaboration with Facilities, IT, and external parties. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Function as a communications hub for department, staying current on, and publishing, as requested, team travel and holiday schedules with ability to locate and contact team members as needed. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Serve as a helpful knowledge base for staff within the department, especially for process and procedures, and provide assistance in a hands-on, proactive manner. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Liaise effectively with Executive Assistant counterparts and build strong working relationships with a wide range of company stakeholders at all levels.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Continually improve processes and procedures to reduce work time and cost without compromising work quality.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;8+ years of relevant experience supporting a Senior Level Executive.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Presentations: Ability to create compelling presentations with design sensibility and impact (i.e.: convert hand-drawn data on a notepad into a visually appealing PowerPoint slide).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
