&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong Linux and Windows administration and engineering experience in enterprise or production environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong hands-on experience with enterprise server hardware, including troubleshooting, lifecycle planning, and firmware management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong experience with enterprise storage and distributed storage systems; Ceph experience strongly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong experience architecting and administering&amp;nbsp;Windows and Linux server platforms&amp;nbsp;in enterprise or production environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong understanding of how storage, compute, and virtualization interact in performance‑sensitive production environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong scripting and automation skills, preferably Python and/or PowerShell.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
